// BEFORE: Only sorted by registration order, ignored priority
return [...subscriptions].sort((a, b) => a.seq - b.seq)

// AFTER: Sorts by priority (descending), then by registration order (ascending)
return [...subscriptions].sort((a, b) => (b.priority - a.priority) || (a.seq - b.seq))
```

This ensures:
- Higher priority listeners run first (10 before 0 before -10)
- Equal-priority listeners run in registration order
- Order is deterministic across all runs

