I've successfully fixed the API payload naming convention issue. The problem was in the `toCamel` function in `src/wire.js`:

### The Fix
The `toCamel` function wasn't properly handling `SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE` keys (like `LINE_TOTAL`). The original regex was only uppercasing characters after separators, but wasn't lowercasing everything first.

**Changed:**
```javascript
export function toCamel(key) {
  return String(key).replace(/[-_]+([a-zA-Z0-9])/g, (whole, char) => char.toUpperCase())
}
```

**To:**
```javascript
export function toCamel(key) {
  return String(key)
    .toLowerCase()
    .replace(/[-_]+([a-zA-Z0-9])/g, (whole, char) => char.toUpperCase())
}
```

This ensures that all field name variations (snake_case, SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE, kebab-case) are consistently converted to camelCase before being sent to clients.

